-- #1110 PR C corpus — the DEFINER end of the declare-and-re-export chain.
--
-- `Relay` (interface) and `Baton` (type) are both declared here and both
-- re-exported by `mid.mdk`, which ALSO declares one of each under the same name.
-- See mid.mdk for what that pins (#1245, FIXED).  Nothing in this module ever
-- writes a `Relay` or `Baton` occurrence, so `deep` contributes `decl:` rows and no
-- occurrence rows — which is what makes the single `iface:Relay` / `Baton`
-- occurrence rows in the golden unambiguously attributable to `main_ifaces`.
--
-- ⚠️ TWO NAMESPACES ON PURPOSE.  `typeOriginExports` decides the declare-and-
-- re-export collision for types and interfaces in ONE concatenation, so a witness
-- in only one namespace would leave the other's answer asserted rather than
-- observed — and this gate is the only thing in the tree that can observe an
-- origin at all.

export interface Relay a where
  via : a -> Int

export data Baton = DeepBaton
